From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: localize placeholder session titles at every display site

New sessions carry the hardcoded English sentinel 'New Session'
(sessionStore optimistic entry, line 112) and the server answers with
'Untitled Session'. Both are data-layer sentinels shared by all locales —
auto-naming (deriveSessionTitle), title-merge protection and empty-session
cleanup pattern-match on them, so they must NOT be rewritten in the store.

Rendering them raw leaked English into every localized UI: zh sidebar and
tab bar showed "Untitled Session"/"New Session" next to fully Chinese
chrome. Sidebar even had a third hardcoded 'Untitled' fallback that was
English-only by construction.

Fix: display-layer mapping. sessionTitle.ts gains
displaySessionTitle(title, localizedFallback) which maps the sentinel set
('', 'New Session', 'Untitled Session') to t('session.untitled') and passes
real titles through. All 10 display sites (Sidebar x3, TabBar, AppShell
mobile header, ActiveSession header, TraceList, TraceSession x3) now route
through it. The data layer is untouched; the obsolete 'tabs.untitled' key
is retired in all five locales in favour of the existing 'session.untitled'
(already translated: 未命名会话 / 未命名會話 / 無題のセッション /
제목 없는 세션). Existing CJK section comments in the locale files and
elsewhere are preserved verbatim — the diff only adds the mapping and
removes the retired key.

Side effect for English users: the tab title no longer flashes between
'New Session' and 'Untitled Session' when fetchSessions() reconciles.

